  "title": "Class-level readings are monotone",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Proved by hand (theorem M): for any network whose other constraints do not involve a leaf's signs, a reading that depends only on the leaves' classes is non-decreasing in each acting bit and constant on non-acting classes, so no class-level reading negates a stored bit. Computed: in a fixed frame (one signing per class) explicit networks read NOT a_1 for cut leaves thin (3,2,2), thin (4,3,2) and Fano, and another signing of a non-acting class makes them read 0; all 718 sigma readings of CLASS-READ-20261110-001 read the frame.",
